      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 American Academy of Dermatology, Inc. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "When the prevention of new lesions fails and when medical therapy of established and growing lesions is ineffective, surgery is the accepted method of dealing with hidradenitis suppurativa/acne inversa. The rationale and preferred techniques of mini-unroofing using a biopsy punch, deroofing using scissors, electrosurgery or laser, and classical wide excision and closure are discussed. The situation in which incision and drainage is considered for temporary pain relief would be best considered an opportunity for deroofing, as illustrated in the accompanying online videos."
      },
